.TH bd 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
bd \- dump one block of a device
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bd
.I "device blkno"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bd
reads block
.I blkno
of
.I device
and prints it as a hexadecimal and character dump.  Blocks are 512
bytes.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH NOTES
A tool for looking at a filesystem by hand: superblocks, inode blocks,
directory blocks, a partition table.  It reads and never writes.
.PP
Reading a block of a mounted, busy filesystem shows what is on the card,
which is not necessarily what the kernel has in its buffers.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# bd /dev/hda2 1        the superblock
# bd /dev/hda 0         the partition table
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR od (1),
.BR fsck (1),
.BR fdisk (1)
